{
  "notes": [
    "Brackets, joist hangers and post bases for timber (mitcad#478): Mitcad's own parts, no supplier, in common sizes; steel plates modelled from their dimensions (no embossing or stiffening ribs), the screw holes cut.",
    "Each is modelled in its mount frame's coordinates (the design's origin and axes): a hanger at the middle of the joist's end on the carrier's face, z into the carrier, x up the joist's section; a bracket on the carrier's face at the middle of the edge where member a's side meets it, z into the carrier, x out of that side; a post base at the middle of the post's end, z into the post, x along its +X.",
    "Holes hole_a_<n> take fasteners into member a (the joist, the post, the member whose end meets), hole_b_<n> into b (the carrier); the generator fills each fasteners entry's frames and count from them.",
    "Steel, hot-dip galvanised: 7850 kg/m3."
  ],
